survey swil1e
#Data from Willie Stanton's Survey Book 1
# p. 51-52	(=PDF p.55-56)

#Typed in by Footleg, June 2012

#30th March 1952
#Tratman's Temple to Sump 1

centreline
cs OSGB:ST 
#Resurveyed by Footleg's TratmansToSump1 surveys, so these legs are kept
#only to connect the rest of the Stanton survey and are not counted in the length.
flags duplicate
date 1952.03.30
# Stanton's bearings come out 3 degrees clockwise of the resurvey even after
# the magnetic declination Therion works out for the date. Measured on his
# streamway books (swildons1-c, d and e, 1952-53) against the resurvey there,
# where it is the same for all three; assumed for his other books.
calibrate compass 3    # back bearings too

#in this survey some angles are in degrees:minutes, others decimal degrees
units tape feet
units depth feet

data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino ignoreall						
B1	AA	78.1	-	293:40	9:30	B1 ('beta' in original notes) is station B1 of page 45, at entrance to "P.G." passage
AA	AB	24.1	115:30	-	-5:30	AA on a big high rock
AB	AC	29.2	-	277:50	0:30	AB on big rock. Stream sinks below boulders.
AC	AD	10.6	121:00	-	22:30	AC on dirty great big rock.
AD	AE	48.3	-	290:00	9:40	Stream rises from boulders.
AE	AF	17	050:30	-	10:20	Stream sinks below boulders.
AF	AG	20.2	-	313:00	3:00	AF above waterfall.
AG	AH	10.1	195:50	-	11:20	
AH	AI	41.6	-	292:10	4:50	
AI	AJ	34.2	138:30	-	6:30	
AJ	AK	31.8	-	286:00	14:30	
AK	AL	11.3	044:00	-	-0:30	AK is below hole into Upper Grottos. Asellus (sp?) present.
#	AL					Total = 1,918'

endcentreline

endsurvey